    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceBase` is the abstract base (not a test), so `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners`, computed from an optional `birthDate` against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (drives DTO generation)\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema \u2192 `OwnerFieldsDto.birthDate`.\n   - Added readOnly `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema \u2192 `OwnerDto.ageBand`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added a derived `getAgeBand()` getter following the existing pattern of `getLocality()`/`getCheckDigit()`: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when no birth date is present so the field is simply absent.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/postgres`, `db/mysql`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against hsqldb; the others are kept consistent.\n\nMapStruct maps `birthDate` (request\u2192entity, entity\u2192response) and the `String` `getAgeBand()` \u2192 the generated enum automatically, exactly as it already does for the `contactPreference` enum. No new function/YAML steps were needed since `birthDate` persists through the existing `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` pipeline and `ageBand` is derived per-response by the mapper, like the other derived fields.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`: birthDate `1990-01-01`, registered today \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
